From 032712e6ede056eaad1d17a9640f511320c7498a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Bainbridge <chris.bainbridge@canonical.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:29:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] test: add unix-session subject coverage to the JS
 authority tests

Add rules test cases that call check_authorization_sync() and
get_admin_identities() with PolkitUnixSession subjects, verifying
that the Subject object exposes the session id, user, groups,
local/active flags and no pid for them. Without the first commit
these test cases abort the test process.

Session subjects need no logind in the test environment: the seat
lookup fails gracefully and subject.seat stays unset, and the
subject's session id comes from the subject itself.

Also add a test for the session monitor change: a unix-session
subject maps to itself in get_session_for_subject().

And document in polkit(8) that subject.pid, subject.system_unit and
subject.no_new_privileges are not set when the subject is a
session.
